---
import ProductImage from '../components/ProductImage.astro';
import '../styles.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<meta name="description" content="Rai Butera. Senior engineer and product builder. Selected work in developer tools, full-stack engineering, and technical leadership." />
<meta name="theme-color" content="#101014" />
<link rel="canonical" href="https://rbutera.com/" />
<title>Rai Butera — Senior engineer. Product builder.</title>
</head><body>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">
        Skip to content
      </a>
      <header class="site-header">
        <a class="wordmark" href="#top">
          Rai Butera.
        </a>
        <button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navigation">Menu</button>
<nav id="navigation" class="navigation" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#work">Work</a><a href="#experience">Experience</a><a href="#about">About</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></nav>
</header>
      <main id="main">
        <section id="top" class="hero" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
          <div class="name-row">
            <h1 id="intro-title">Rai Butera.</h1>
            <p class="eyebrow name-note">
              Engineering
              <br />
              Products
              <br />
              Better software
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-body">
            <div class="hero-copy">
              <h2>
                Senior engineer.
                <br />
                Product builder.
              </h2>
              <p>
                I build products and the tools to make complex software easier
                to ship and review.
              </p>
              <div class="actions">
                <a class="button primary" href="#work">
                  Explore my work
                </a>
                <a class="text-link" href="#contact">
                  Get in touch
                </a>
              </div>
              <p class="eyebrow hero-footnote">
                Ideas
                <br />
                Systems
                <br />
                People
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-art">
              <img src="/images/hero-grid.png" alt="" fetchpriority="high" />
              <span class="eyebrow art-caption">
                Build
                <br />
                Review
                <br />
                Ship
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <nav class="work-strip" aria-label="Selected work">
            <a href="#rennet">Rennet</a>
            <a href="#chaching">Chaching</a>
            <a href="#easyjet">
              easyJet <span>via Focused Labs</span>
            </a>
            <a href="#lexstep">LexStep</a>
          </nav>
        </section>
        <div id="work">
          <section
            id="rennet"
            class="project section"
            aria-labelledby="rennet-title"
          >
            <div class="project-heading reveal">
              <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">01 / Independent product</p>
                <h2 id="rennet-title">Rennet</h2>
                <h3>
                  Making code
                  <br class="desktop-break" /> review keep up.
                </h3>
              </div>
              <p class="eyebrow marginal-note">
                Code
                <br />
                Context
                <br />
                Better decisions
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-intro reveal">
              <p>
                I built Rennet to make large changes easier to understand,
                question, and review.
              </p>
              <a
                class="button primary"
                href="https://rennet.dev/"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noreferrer"
              >
                Explore Rennet
              </a>
            </div>
            <figure class="project-figure reveal">
              <ProductImage
                src="/images/rennet-review.png"
                alt="Rennet review showing engineering decisions linked to source code"
              />
              <figcaption>
                Decisions, rationale, and the code behind them. An existing
                product capture.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
            <div class="project-detail">
              <p class="eyebrow">The work behind the interface</p>
              <p>
                Generating more code makes understanding the change more
                important. Rennet brings specialised review lenses and
                source-linked evidence into a local-first workspace, so the
                reasoning stays beside the work.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>
          <section
            id="chaching"
            class="project section chaching"
            aria-labelledby="chaching-title"
          >
            <div class="project-heading reveal">
              <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">02 / Independent product</p>
                <h2 id="chaching-title">Chaching</h2>
                <h3>
                  Your agents run.
                  <br />
                  The meter does too.
                </h3>
              </div>
              <p class="eyebrow marginal-note">
                Token spend
                <br />
                Cache hits
                <br />
                Actual receipts
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-intro reveal">
              <p>
                A cash register for coding agents. I built Chaching to make
                token spend and cache costs visible, from the terminal to the
                receipt.
              </p>
              <a
                class="button primary"
                href="https://chaching.fyi/"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noreferrer"
              >
                Explore Chaching
              </a>
            </div>
            <div class="chaching-images reveal">
              <figure>
                <ProductImage
                  src="/images/chaching-dashboard.png"
                  alt="Chaching dashboard showing daily token spend and account usage"
                />
                <figcaption>
                  The dashboard. Spend across tools, at a glance.
                </figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure class="receipt">
                <ProductImage
                  src="/images/chaching-receipt.png"
                  alt="Chaching sample receipt itemising token spend and cache savings"
                />
                <figcaption>And yes, it prints a receipt.</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
            <div class="project-detail">
              <p class="eyebrow">Accounting with a point of view</p>
              <p>
                Cache reads and writes still cost money. Chaching makes those
                details legible through a live terminal dashboard, a web view,
                and a shareable receipt. The screenshots show example product
                data.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
        <section
          id="experience"
          class="section experience"
          aria-labelledby="experience-title"
        >
          <p class="eyebrow">03 / Commercial work</p>
          <h2 id="experience-title">
            Built with teams.
            <br />
            Shipped into production.
          </h2>
          <article id="easyjet" class="experience-row reveal">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Senior full-stack engineering</p>
              <h3>easyJet</h3>
              <p class="muted">via Focused Labs</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4>Modernising while delivering.</h4>
              <p>
                Production features from the first week. React and TypeScript on
                the frontend, C# and .NET behind it. I helped move the codebase
                into Nx in reviewable steps, with shared libraries used by three
                frontends and a Playwright/MSW crash-detection gate.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article id="lexstep" class="experience-row reveal">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Tech Lead / 2020–2025</p>
              <h3>LexStep</h3>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4>Leading a platform through change.</h4>
              <p>
                I led an international team through a legacy-platform overhaul:
                tested NestJS services, a MySQL-to-PostgreSQL migration, React
                adoption, and infrastructure moving from VMs and Jenkins to AWS
                and Terraform. The responsibility included the incidents, not
                just the releases.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </section>
        <section
          id="about"
          class="section about"
          aria-labelledby="about-title"
        >
          <p class="eyebrow">04 / A little context</p>
          <div>
            <h2 id="about-title">
              I like knowing
              <br />
              how things work.
            </h2>
            <p>
              And making them work better. My experience spans full-stack
              engineering, technical leadership, and building my own products. I
              care about the decisions underneath the interface as much as the
              interface itself.
            </p>
            <p>
              Rennet and Chaching come from problems I run into in my own work.
              Building and using them keeps that feedback loop short.
            </p>
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="https://github.com/rbutera"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
            >
              Find me on GitHub
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section
          id="contact"
          class="section contact"
          aria-labelledby="contact-title"
        >
          <p class="eyebrow">Have something in mind?</p>
          <h2 id="contact-title">
            Let’s build
            <br />
            something good.
          </h2>
          <a class="contact-email" href="mailto:rai@rbutera.com">
            rai@rbutera.com
          </a>
          <p>
            Engineering roles, interesting projects, and good conversations.
          </p>
        </section>
      </main>
      <footer>
        <a href="#top">Rai Butera.</a>
        <span class="eyebrow">© 2026</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/rbutera" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          GitHub
        </a>
        <a href="#top">Back to top</a>
      </footer>
    <script src="../interactions.js"></script>
</body></html>
